--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,49 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkeys
+
+After signing in, readers can open **Account settings** from the header at
+`/devtools-times/account/settings`. The passkey section lists registered keys,
+their provider, creation date, and last sign-in. Readers can create a passkey,
+rename its account label, or confirm its removal. Password sign-in remains
+available after removing the final key.
+
+Password authentication still uses the existing Times login service, through a
+same-origin endpoint that establishes an HttpOnly Astro session. Passkey registration
+and authentication are verified on the server with SimpleWebAuthn. Accounts, public
+keys, signature counters, and single-use, five-minute challenges are persisted in
+SQLite; the browser never receives public-key records or signature counters.
+This app previously had no credential store, so new accounts start with an empty list.
+
+Use Node.js 22.13 or later (Node.js 24 recommended). Set these **runtime environment
+variables** for your deployment:
+
+| Variable | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` | `https://astro-news-pytrpecapa-uc.a.run.app` | Exact public HTTPS origin, without a path. |
+| `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID` | Hostname of the configured origin | Fixed relying-party ID shared by registration, sign-in, and synchronization. Set explicitly when using a parent domain. |
+| `PASSKEY_DB_PATH` | `./data/passkeys.sqlite` | Credential database location. Mount durable storage here and retain it across releases. |
+
+Keep the configured origin/RP ID stable after registering keys. The settings page
+uses the server's RP ID and Base64URL user/credential identifiers for WebAuthn
+`signalAllAcceptedCredentials`, on load and after deletion (including an empty
+list). Browsers without the Signal API retain full server-side management and
+show instructions to remove stale keys in their password manager. A per-key
+nickname is an account label; it does not change the WebAuthn user's profile.
+
+The SQLite implementation supports Node processes sharing one local database file.
+Multiple application replicas need a shared account/credential database and shared
+Astro session storage; do not deploy independent ephemeral credential files.
+The Node adapter's default session storage is filesystem-backed.
+
+Provider hints and icons are a small local subset of the
+[passkey-authenticator-aaguids registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids).
+Unknown or zero AAGUIDs use a generic key icon; provider metadata never authorizes access.
+
+`pnpm test` runs server-handler and browser API unit tests without opening a browser
+or starting a server. It includes a software authenticator that registers a real
+P-256 public key and signs assertions to exercise cryptographic verification.
+`pnpm run build` builds the app. `pnpm check` checks the whole project; unrelated
+existing image/content and navigation type errors are still present.
